        "attempt": 1,
        "status": "OK",
        "duration_seconds": 62.291,
        "asr_text": "AI news is now telling two stories at once. AI systems are becoming better at difficult, multi-step work. At the same time, safety tests are asking a harder question: what happens when a capable system meets a weak boundary? From November 2023 to October 2025, a UK safety institute tested more than 30 advanced AI systems in cyber tasks close to the level of a new worker. Average success rose from just over 10% to about 50%. In 2025, the first system in these tests completed expert-level cyber tasks. The best systems also completed software tasks estimated to take a human expert more than one hour, with success above 40%. These were controlled tests. They show measured growth in the tested abilities. They do not show general autonomy or a loss of human control.",
